From 1e9c1a8eb0c56f1693f8b8a9a0e581bceab2edaa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 04:53:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02269/11362] [outer-loop] require both
 engine()+is_level_complete() in induced code; honest finding: gemma-4-12B too
 weak

E3-in-agent pipeline now runs END-TO-END on the local GPU model (server, multi-round
refactor, parse-validate, robust) -- but the HONEST result is model-quality-bound:
gemma-4-12B induced a 0% world model for cd82 (engine returned a SCALAR not a 64x64 grid;
omitted is_level_complete). codex was 27%. NEITHER clears the divergence. So 'does accuracy
climb enough?' = NO yet -- the refactor loop works but base induction quality is the wall.
Added a contract check (require both functions -> retry). NEXT levers (now unblocked by the
GPU fix): benchmark the STRONGER open models (gemma-4-26B-A4B, Qwen3.6-35B-A3B) + a runtime
contract smoke-test (reject scalar-returning engines). The verifier-grounding correctly
refused to trust the 0% model (no plan, no fabricated solve).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 python/carnot/agentic/arc_executable_world_model.py | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/python/carnot/agentic/arc_executable_world_model.py b/python/carnot/agentic/arc_executable_world_model.py
index 04fc900194..0e4fdd3a39 100644
--- a/python/carnot/agentic/arc_executable_world_model.py
+++ b/python/carnot/agentic/arc_executable_world_model.py
@@ -383,8 +383,8 @@ class LocalGGUFProposer:
             except Exception as e:
                 return False, f"local gguf (GPU server) failed: {e!r}"[:200]
             code = _extract_python(text)
-            if not code or "def engine" not in code:
-                last = "no engine() in output"; continue
+            if not code or "def engine" not in code or "def is_level_complete" not in code:
+                last = "missing engine() or is_level_complete() in output"; continue
             try:
                 ast.parse(code)               # never write/use code that doesn't parse
             except SyntaxError as se:
